WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.602
-Thank you, and God bless.

00:00:04.103 --> 00:00:05.204
Actually, one more thing.

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:06.739
Actually reminds me of a story

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:09.108
I once heard from one of my --
my friend Tim.

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:11.244
We used to call him
Duke Suitcase.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:12.746
[ Laughter ]
That's funny, right?

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:14.046 line:0%
-That's great.
-Yes.

00:00:14.046 --> 00:00:16.048 line:0%
-Should we just do it
one more time from the top?

00:00:16.048 --> 00:00:22.221 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:24.890
So, tonight is President Biden's
first address to Congress,

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:28.861
so we're gonna spoof that before
he actually does the speech,

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:31.197
which is always tricky to do.
To work on the impression,

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.832
we have one of our researchers
put together a reel

00:00:33.832 --> 00:00:36.402
of speeches of Joe Biden,
and I will just play it

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:39.271
over and over again so I can
practice things he does,

00:00:39.271 --> 00:00:41.607
little nuances, things...

00:00:41.607 --> 00:00:44.978
you know, the way his voice is
and the way he moves his hands,

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:46.979
just so I can kind of get
a general idea

00:00:46.979 --> 00:00:50.116
of how to do an impersonation
of President Joe Biden.

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:52.452
-Earlier today,
as was referenced,

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:56.088
I participated in the first
meeting of the G7 leaders.

00:00:56.088 --> 00:00:57.423
-Tomorrow...
-It's about investing

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:59.758
in infrastructure...
-Got both of the hands.

00:00:59.758 --> 00:01:02.394
He does a lot of eye wiping,
I will say.

00:01:02.394 --> 00:01:04.897
-Remember that old proverb,
"For want of a nail"...

00:01:04.897 --> 00:01:07.367
-Remember that old...
It's kind of like "'member?"

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.335
Almost like
he just got over a cold.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.104
And he's kind of like...

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:12.671
He's very innocent standing.

00:01:12.671 --> 00:01:15.508
He almost feels like one of
the Little Rascals or something.

00:01:15.508 --> 00:01:19.345
Like he just ate the last cookie
or something.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:22.314
-Workers and corporate leaders,
Republicans and Democrats.

00:01:22.314 --> 00:01:25.317
-Ohhh...it's very nasally,
which is what I am anyway,

00:01:25.317 --> 00:01:27.486
so I can probably do that.

00:01:27.486 --> 00:01:29.155
He wears some decent
pocket squares

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:30.823
with little points

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:33.559
that I know our wardrobe
can knock out.

00:01:33.559 --> 00:01:35.394
But let me just see -- let me
hear his voice again.

00:01:35.394 --> 00:01:37.463
Like, which is...
-United States is determined...

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:40.466
It's like...all of a sudden...
[ Coughs ]

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:43.802
-...in the history [coughs]
of the United States of America.

00:01:43.802 --> 00:01:44.971
[ Coughs ] Excuse me.

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.406
-[ Coughing ]
-You know, in this battle

00:01:46.406 --> 00:01:48.241
[coughs] for the soul
of America...

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.410
-I just said that.
[ Laughing ] That's crazy.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.744
That's -- Alright.

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:55.514
I think our take on Biden
has been

00:01:55.514 --> 00:01:59.818
these kind of stories
that he has, you know,

00:01:59.818 --> 00:02:02.655
that relate to the subject
that he's talking about,

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:05.290
but sometimes the stories
are too long

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:06.959
and a little bizarre.

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:09.729
You know, like,
"I knew a guy named --

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:12.799
who used to be called
Mississippi Jack.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:17.403
And -- And he would -- He'd --
He would climb up a flagpole

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:22.308
and -- and stand next to it
horizontally,

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:25.645
and he could hold -- and he
could pretend he's a human flag.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:28.314
And we would all go out and --
and salute him."

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:29.782
Something that bizarre.

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:32.785
Of course, he doesn't do that,
but that's the whole joke of it.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.121
I've been watching this, like,
for an hour.

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:39.124
It's 1:30, and we have to do
the show at 5:00.

00:02:39.124 --> 00:02:42.361
But we're gonna pre-tape this
probably around 2:30.

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:44.864
So, we have a good script.
I think it's really funny.

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:47.200
I got to get a wig and makeup
and all that.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.735
-What's going on?
-Ah, alright. Here we go.

00:02:49.735 --> 00:02:52.371
Step into
the hair and makeup room.

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:54.373
Here we go. And we're not gonna
fast-forward this.

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:56.542
We're gonna do it in real time,
so get ready

00:02:56.542 --> 00:02:59.812
for two hours of great
behind-the-scenes footage.

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:05.217 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:06.286
So much work went into it,

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:07.954
and you can't tell
when you watch it.

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:12.625 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.961
Look at this,
it's already happening.

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:19.131 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:19.131 --> 00:03:21.434
When I was a kid, if you wanted
to get across a river,

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:24.437
you'd have to try a long jump.

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:26.105
I knew you would do
the pocket square.

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.441
I just knew it.
I didn't even have to ask you.

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.442
I knew it, knew it, knew it.
Yes!

00:03:30.442 --> 00:03:32.444
Holy moly.

00:03:32.444 --> 00:03:34.446
What? How?

00:03:34.446 --> 00:03:37.450
It's just insane,
the attention to detail.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.619 line:0%
-We added the stripe
in the middle here

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:43.623 line:0%
with ribbons to create
the same type of tie.

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:53.632 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:53.632 --> 00:03:55.134 line:0%
-Hey, bud.
-You look great.

00:03:55.134 --> 00:03:56.802 line:0%
-Nice, huh?
-My God.

00:03:56.802 --> 00:03:58.671 line:0%
-Crazy, right?
-That's so crazy.

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:00.006
-[Speaking indistinctly]

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:01.841
-Alright, let's do it.
-Thanks, bud.

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:05.177
[ All speaking indistinctly ]

00:04:05.177 --> 00:04:06.845
-[ Coughs ] Excuse me.

00:04:06.845 --> 00:04:08.881
[ Coughs ]
-Like this, yeah.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:13.019
-So, tighten up that background?

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:15.020
-At Addison Creek?

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:16.756
-Addison Creek, you said?
-Yeah.

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:18.858
We'd catch this big --
I don't know why.

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.726
-[ Laughs ] It's funny.
I don't know why.

00:04:20.726 --> 00:04:22.261
-Big -- Big catch.

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:24.096
Who could get the big catch

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:25.597
at Addison's "crick"?

00:04:25.597 --> 00:04:28.101
Is it gonna be like, "And now,
President Joe Biden"?

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:30.069
-I think so, and then
we're gonna white-flash.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:32.071
We're showing the best moments.
-Oh, I see.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:33.573
-Would it be funny if,
towards the end,

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:36.075
we both stand perfectly still
with our arms stretched out?

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:38.578
Try to outlast the other.
Like, we act it out.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:40.613
And then we just, like,
latch onto that.

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.281
-Yeah, that's funny.

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:45.117
We'd both stand perfectly still
with our arms out,

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:46.952
try to outlast Joe.

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:48.287
-Great.
-Good.

00:04:48.287 --> 00:04:49.455
-Okay, great.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:50.623
-How was it, how was it,
how was it?

00:04:50.623 --> 00:04:52.958
Hey, guys.
-Great job.

00:04:52.958 --> 00:04:55.294
-I think by the end
I kind of got better into it.

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:56.863
The character, right?

00:04:56.863 --> 00:04:58.864
-[ Laughing ] The suitcase.

00:04:58.864 --> 00:05:00.800
-Duke Suitcase?
[ All chuckling ]

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.969
That was Brad and Nick, but I --

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:05.304
We cut it out, but I'm like,
"We got to go back and do it."

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:13.379 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:15.381
Alright, so we did the sketch.

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:17.216
I think I got there
more towards the end of it,

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:19.385
but now it's up to the editors
and the writers

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:22.721
and, you know, our producer
to make sure we have

00:05:22.721 --> 00:05:24.523
the right takes on everything,

00:05:24.523 --> 00:05:27.126
and then we'll play it in front
of an audience and see

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:28.494
what happens, see what sticks.

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:30.496
Alright, I got to go get ready
for a monologue.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.831
Bye!

00:05:32.831 --> 00:05:34.199
[ Cheers and applause ]
-♪ We will rock you ♪

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:36.836
♪ You, you, you,
the legendary Roots crew ♪

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:38.937
-Earlier tonight,
President Biden addressed

00:05:38.937 --> 00:05:41.941
a joint session of Congress
for the first time as president.

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:44.310
It was a great speech,
and in case you missed it,

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:47.146
we put together some of the more
interesting moments.

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:48.981
Check it out.

00:05:48.981 --> 00:05:52.985
-Ladies and gentlemen, the
President of the United States.

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:55.454
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:58.424
-Madam Speaker,
Madam Vice President,

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:01.260
members of Congress,
my fellow Americans,

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:04.497
tomorrow marks the first 100
days of my presidency,

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:07.099
and our vaccine rollout has been
a big success.

00:06:07.099 --> 00:06:10.569
Over 200 million Americans
have gotten at least one dose,

00:06:10.569 --> 00:06:13.339
and I tell you, modern medicine
sure has changed a lot

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:15.341
from back when I was a kid.

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:18.310
Used to be you'd go to your
doctor and say,

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:21.347
"Listen, Jack, I got my knees
all scraped up

00:06:21.347 --> 00:06:24.016
trying to catch a big earthworm,

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:27.386
use it to get the biggest catch
over at Addison Creek."

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:29.154
[ Coughs ]

00:06:29.154 --> 00:06:31.757
Excuse me.

00:06:31.757 --> 00:06:33.625
[ Coughs ]

00:06:33.625 --> 00:06:36.795
Thank you, and God bless.

00:06:36.795 --> 00:06:39.799
Actually, one more thing.

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:41.967
Actually reminds me of a story
I once heard

00:06:41.967 --> 00:06:43.435
from my friend named Tim.

00:06:43.435 --> 00:06:45.704
His nickname was Duke Suitcase.

00:06:45.704 --> 00:06:48.040
-This has been the President
of the United States.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.375
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.043
-[ Laughing ]
What's he talking about?

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:52.711
Duke Suitcase?

00:06:52.711 --> 00:06:53.913
Stick around.
We'll be right back.

